(676332, 70626, 18191, '<td valign="top">Australia---I LOVE it and i can''t wait until i go there this summer. Great shot, I love the sun coming through the clouds---definitely one of my favorites.</td>', 'Australia---I LOVE it and i can''t wait until i go there this summer. Great shot, I love the sun coming through the clouds---definitely one of my favorites.', '2004-04-19 19:37:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(676338, 70268, 19376, '<td valign="top">awesome shot-nice contrast-between black and white-and red---awesome-if i could vote--a definate 9-10<br/></td>', 'awesome shot-nice contrast-between black and white-and red---awesome-if i could vote--a definate 9-10', '2004-04-19 19:40:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(676339, 70201, 19608, '<td valign="top">Colors are VERY effectice.  Slim Jim framing is great for the image.  Birds are well placed and have a nice relationship.</td>', 'Colors are VERY effectice.  Slim Jim framing is great for the image.  Birds are well placed and have a nice relationship.', '2004-04-19 19:40:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(676340, 70642, 19608, '<td valign="top">Very nice graphic!  Background adds a lot to the overall feel to this image.  Reflections on the water are nice.</td>', 'Very nice graphic!  Background adds a lot to the overall feel to this image.  Reflections on the water are nice.', '2004-04-19 19:40:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(676342, 70914, 19608, '<td valign="top">Perfect placement of the statue in front of the building - extremely effective.  The dark sky behind the building complements the darkness of the horse and rider - another great feature.  Finally, the color in the top of the building and the flags/wall plaques  add a lot to the overall image.  There are just 2 very minor detractors for me:  1) I''d like to rotate the entire image a bit counter-clockwise. 2) The tree in the bottom right corner is a bit detracting - have a chain saw?  Even so - this image is in my top three so far, way to go!</td>', 'Perfect placement of the statue in front of the building - extremely effective.  The dark sky behind the building complements the darkness of the horse and rider - another great feature.  Finally, the color in the top of the building and the flags/wall plaques  add a lot to the overall image.  There are just 2 very minor detractors for me:  1) I''d like to rotate the entire image a bit counter-clockwise. 2) The tree in the bottom right corner is a bit detracting - have a chain saw?  Even so - this image is in my top three so far, way to go!', '2004-04-19 19:41:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(676343, 70370, 19376, '<td valign="top">crazy cool shot-awesom!! 10 if i could vote!! great job</td>', 'crazy cool shot-awesom!! 10 if i could vote!! great job', '2004-04-19 19:41:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(676347, 70935, 12998, '<td valign="top">All I can say is WOW, nice model, nice lines and lighting</td>', 'All I can say is WOW, nice model, nice lines and lighting', '2004-04-19 19:49:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(676379, 70699, 19376, '<td valign="top">would have been an awesome shot....way to grainy...great shot nonetheless</td>', 'would have been an awesome shot....way to grainy...great shot nonetheless', '2004-04-19 20:21:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(676413, 70566, 12131, '<td valign="top">I hope you score high if not a ribbon.  Beautiful shot.  I even like the border, it helps give continuity to the light at the center.  How were you able to get the light to work while shooting directly into it though?  I''ve tried but it comes out too bright or too obscure. Anyway, 10 from me.</td>', 'I hope you score high if not a ribbon.  Beautiful shot.  I even like the border, it helps give continuity to the light at the center.  How were you able to get the light to work while shooting directly into it though?  I''ve tried but it comes out too bright or too obscure. Anyway, 10 from me.', '2004-04-19 20:53:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(676415, 70858, 12131, '<td valign="top">I love the blue and the slope.  If anything I wish it was brighter.  8</td>', 'I love the blue and the slope.  If anything I wish it was brighter.  8', '2004-04-19 20:54:47.000000', NULL, 1),
