(685841, 70302, 12160, '<td valign="top">beautiful image... congrats on the win!</td>', 'beautiful image... congrats on the win!', '2004-04-26 13:49:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(685870, 70302, 15207, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on this ribbon. Not to take anything away from the other ribbon winners, but I really thought this would get the blue. After all, it''s incredibly hard to get this close to these birds and you can''t exactly pose the shot. This could almost have worked for serendipity! I am absolutely shocked and horrified that you had a single 1 or even two 4s! Anyway... congrats on the high ranking. You really deserved it. Looking forward to seeing more of your work.</td>', 'Congratulations on this ribbon. Not to take anything away from the other ribbon winners, but I really thought this would get the blue. After all, it''s incredibly hard to get this close to these birds and you can''t exactly pose the shot. This could almost have worked for serendipity! I am absolutely shocked and horrified that you had a single 1 or even two 4s! Anyway... congrats on the high ranking. You really deserved it. Looking forward to seeing more of your work.', '2004-04-26 14:11:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(685880, 70503, 1717, '<td valign="top">beautiful!  congrats on such a great capture and a well deserved ribbon!</td>', 'beautiful!  congrats on such a great capture and a well deserved ribbon!', '2004-04-26 14:16:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(685933, 70925, 5112, '<td valign="top">I  must say that I did not pay much attention to this photo during the challenge, but now, when I look at it, I find all sorts of things that I like in it:<br/>the low horizon line<br/>the little white backlight behind the blackish outcrop<br/>the barely there mountains<br/>the beautiful clouds<br/>the (at least to my eyes) slightly purplish tint<br/> <br/>All in all, a beautiful shot, one that can grow on you.<br/></td>', 'I  must say that I did not pay much attention to this photo during the challenge, but now, when I look at it, I find all sorts of things that I like in it:the low horizon linethe little white backlight behind the blackish outcropthe barely there mountainsthe beautiful cloudsthe (at least to my eyes) slightly purplish tint All in all, a beautiful shot, one that can grow on you.', '2004-04-26 14:32:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(685984, 70642, 3032, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by darcy:</b></div><hr/><i> But I have to ask, how can your aperature be so large - 1.8 - when your depth of field seems to be so deep.  Doesn''t a large aperature usually give a shallow depth of field? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>"At a fixed aperture, focussing at a greater distance brings more of the foreground and background into the zone of sharpness." quote from National Geographic''s Photography Field Guide.<br/> <br/>The usual dramatic small DOF of a 50mm @ F1.8 is mostly seen with portraits shot from a relative close range. The focus point here is considerably further away.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by darcy: But I have to ask, how can your aperature be so large - 1.8 - when your depth of field seems to be so deep.  Doesn''t a large aperature usually give a shallow depth of field?   "At a fixed aperture, focussing at a greater distance brings more of the foreground and background into the zone of sharpness." quote from National Geographic''s Photography Field Guide. The usual dramatic small DOF of a 50mm @ F1.8 is mostly seen with portraits shot from a relative close range. The focus point here is considerably further away. ', '2004-04-26 14:56:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(685995, 70503, 12252, '<td valign="top">Congrats, but I''m sorry, you couldn''t have taken that picture without a dSLR! Just kidding! Super image, great job, and enjoy your ribbon!</td>', 'Congrats, but I''m sorry, you couldn''t have taken that picture without a dSLR! Just kidding! Super image, great job, and enjoy your ribbon!', '2004-04-26 15:02:21.000000', NULL, 0),
