(686470, 70503, 20395, '<td valign="top">I was going through your entries for past challenges, and I was struck by how much your photography has improved since your first submissions! Way to go! Enjoy your ribbon!</td>', 'I was going through your entries for past challenges, and I was struck by how much your photography has improved since your first submissions! Way to go! Enjoy your ribbon!', '2004-04-26 20:58:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(686502, 70710, 714, '<td valign="top">Your welcome!  This is a stunning shot.</td>', 'Your welcome!  This is a stunning shot.', '2004-04-26 21:15:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(686566, 70724, 20324, '<td valign="top">This was my first entry a  the DPChallange, so I read the requirements of Advance Editing and the description of the theme (...take a photo that has a silhouette as part of your composition) My original shot is below.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=72498" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/20324/thumb/72498.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/20324/thumb/72498.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/20324/thumb/72498.jpg"/></a> <br/>I underexposed it to pull out more of the silhouette of the dogs muzzle, chest and front leg, then corrected the contrast, added a little bit texture and cropped it. Did I change it a lot? I chose this shot because I liked the composition created by the dog''s body and its shadow. I like the paint texture I created. In my opinion it gives softer and more artistic sensation. I was pretty disappointed at the beginning with the low score, but after reading some discussions on the forums I realized that my definition of photography was much broader then generally accepted on DPChallenge. I understand that some people don''t like dogs or effects applied, but discussion about integrity of the photograph is valid only if one can see the original picture, otherwise it is only gossip. My judgment of a photograph, at first is based on the emotions I feel are being portrayed, then I analyze the composition, color and technical characteristics of the work. Additionally, if it is a contest on a particular topic, like on the  DPChallenge, it is important to adhere to the subject.<br/>So far I have enjoyed the site a lot. Thank you for taking your time to read this and for all your comments. I hope to learn a lot here.<br/>Cheers, <br/>Art<br/></td>', 'This was my first entry a  the DPChallange, so I read the requirements of Advance Editing and the description of the theme (...take a photo that has a silhouette as part of your composition) My original shot is below. I underexposed it to pull out more of the silhouette of the dogs muzzle, chest and front leg, then corrected the contrast, added a little bit texture and cropped it. Did I change it a lot? I chose this shot because I liked the composition created by the dog''s body and its shadow. I like the paint texture I created. In my opinion it gives softer and more artistic sensation. I was pretty disappointed at the beginning with the low score, but after reading some discussions on the forums I realized that my definition of photography was much broader then generally accepted on DPChallenge. I understand that some people don''t like dogs or effects applied, but discussion about integrity of the photograph is valid only if one can see the original picture, otherwise it is only gossip. My judgment of a photograph, at first is based on the emotions I feel are being portrayed, then I analyze the composition, color and technical characteristics of the work. Additionally, if it is a contest on a particular topic, like on the  DPChallenge, it is important to adhere to the subject.So far I have enjoyed the site a lot. Thank you for taking your time to read this and for all your comments. I hope to learn a lot here.Cheers, Art', '2004-04-26 21:49:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(686571, 70503, 11078, '<td valign="top">Hi to you all <br/> <br/>Just to say a Big ''Thank you'' to all the kind people and nice words regarding my silhouette image. I am really proud of it and it has definately given me a buzz winning a blue ribbon.<br/>I strive for perfection and I think this was one of those rare moments I was very lucky to be in the right place at the right time and to be able to use my camera in the right way. The weather was just perfect.<br/>I love my little camera and it has given me heaps of pleasure I really enjoy belonging to D P C and I have found  really nice people who write to me regulary through this site.<br/>I am sure my photography has improved and I find myself looking at the world in a very different way. I think sometimes my family think I have lost the plot when we are out for walks and I drift off to photograph a flower or whatever but I do enjoy it very much. Some of the challenges I have had to really struggle with but apart from one that I down loaded wrong onto the site I think I am definately a much improved <br/>photographer. <br/>So Thank you once again for the vote and for making my day a happy one <br/>I had my brother in law from the U K with me when I took the silhouette image and he was going back to the U K so I quickly got Imageland in Hamilton to run off a copy for him to take home. the manager at Imageland liked it so much that he wanted to print it off on canvas ( it was the first he has done on his new machine) I think the size is 24inchs x 18 inchs (not sure I think thats right) and he has framed it and put it on show It looks fantastic on canvas, he is not selling it and it has my (c) and name on it proudly displayed in the shop window.<br/>I''ll get off my soap box now LOL! <br/>Thanks again<br/>Regards<br/>Sally</td>', 'Hi to you all  Just to say a Big ''Thank you'' to all the kind people and nice words regarding my silhouette image. I am really proud of it and it has definately given me a buzz winning a blue ribbon.I strive for perfection and I think this was one of those rare moments I was very lucky to be in the right place at the right time and to be able to use my camera in the right way. The weather was just perfect.I love my little camera and it has given me heaps of pleasure I really enjoy belonging to D P C and I have found  really nice people who write to me regulary through this site.I am sure my photography has improved and I find myself looking at the world in a very different way. I think sometimes my family think I have lost the plot when we are out for walks and I drift off to photograph a flower or whatever but I do enjoy it very much. Some of the challenges I have had to really struggle with but apart from one that I down loaded wrong onto the site I think I am definately a much improved photographer. So Thank you once again for the vote and for making my day a happy one I had my brother in law from the U K with me when I took the silhouette image and he was going back to the U K so I quickly got Imageland in Hamilton to run off a copy for him to take home. the manager at Imageland liked it so much that he wanted to print it off on canvas ( it was the first he has done on his new machine) I think the size is 24inchs x 18 inchs (not sure I think thats right) and he has framed it and put it on show It looks fantastic on canvas, he is not selling it and it has my (c) and name on it proudly displayed in the shop window.I''ll get off my soap box now LOL! Thanks againRegardsSally', '2004-04-26 22:03:25.000000', NULL, 0),
